.TH REFQUILL 1 "October 15, 2026" "Refquill" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
refquill \- generate portable PHP, TypeScript, and Rust API references
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
refquill init [--config PATH] [--language LANGUAGE]
refquill generate [CONFIG] [--force]
refquill validate FILE
refquill schema --output DIRECTORY
refquill help [COMMAND]
refquill --help
refquill --version
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Refquill analyzes configured PHP, TypeScript, and Rust inputs and writes one
portable schema-v1 JSON API document. The document contains declarations,
documentation, types, relationships, diagnostics, and source locations.
.PP
The npm CLI requires Node.js 22.18 or newer. PHP analysis uses the bundled
Rust executable and Mago; PHP and Composer are not required. TypeScript
analysis uses the bundled TypeDoc and TypeScript compiler.
.PP
Rust inputs can import an existing rustdoc JSON file in format 61 or invoke
Cargo with a compatible nightly toolchain. Cargo generation executes the
project's build scripts and procedural macros; imported JSON does not.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a small language-specific configuration. The default file is
refquill.json in the current directory. An existing file is never overwritten.
.EX
refquill init --language php
refquill init --language typescript --config frontend.json
refquill init --language rust
.EE
.TP
.B generate [CONFIG]
Analyze every configured input and write the configured output. CONFIG defaults
to refquill.json in the current directory. Configuration paths are resolved
relative to the configuration file; sourceRoot defaults to its directory.
.IP "" 7
Output is deterministic. Identical output is left untouched. Failed analysis
preserves the previous artifact. An unmanaged or edited regular output file
requires an explicit --force. Symlinks and non-regular outputs are rejected.
.EX
refquill generate
refquill generate docs/refquill.json
refquill generate refquill.json --force
.EE
.TP
.B validate FILE
Validate a schema-v1 artifact's schema, symbol graph, source paths, and
integrity fingerprint. Invalid or edited artifacts return a failure status.
.EX
refquill validate docs/api.generated.json
.EE
.TP
.B schema
Write document.schema.json, resolved.schema.json, and config.schema.json to
the required output directory, creating that directory if necessary.
Existing schema files in that directory are replaced.
.EX
refquill schema --output schemas
.EE
.TP
.B help [COMMAND]
Print top-level help, or help for a named command.
.EX
refquill help
refquill help generate
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Common options
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help for the CLI or a command.
.EX
refquill --help
refquill generate --help
.EE
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the CLI version. This option belongs to the top-level CLI.
.EX
refquill --version
.EE
.SS Init options
.TP
.B --config PATH
Write the new configuration at PATH. Default: refquill.json.
The parent directory must already exist. The command refuses to overwrite
any existing file.
.EX
refquill init --config backend.json
.EE
.TP
.B --language LANGUAGE
Select php, typescript, or rust. Default: php. The generated PHP configuration
selects src; TypeScript selects tsconfig.json and src/index.ts; Rust selects
Cargo.toml with the nightly toolchain. Edit the configuration before generation.
.EX
refquill init --language typescript
.EE
.SS Generate options
.TP
.B --force
Allow replacement of an unmanaged or edited regular output file. Use when
adopting existing output. This does not permit
overwriting source files, configuration, symlinks, or non-regular files.
.EX
refquill generate refquill.json --force
.EE
.SS Schema options
.TP
.B --output DIRECTORY
Required. Write the three JSON Schema files to DIRECTORY.
.EX
refquill schema --output schemas
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B refquill.json
Default configuration. It specifies the output .json file and one or more named
language inputs. It may also set title, sourceRoot, includeProtected,
and exclude.
.TP
.B docs/api.generated.json
Output path selected by init's generated configuration. Consumers validate
or resolve this artifact with @nickwelsh/refquill-schema and render it with
@nickwelsh/refquill-fumadocs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REFQUILL_BINARY
Override the native executable used by the npm wrapper. Otherwise the wrapper
uses a locally staged binary or the installed optional platform package.
.TP
.B REFQUILL_NODE
Node executable used for TypeScript analysis when running the native CLI
directly. The npm wrapper sets this to its own Node executable.
.TP
.B REFQUILL_TYPESCRIPT_WORKER
Path to the TypeScript worker when running the native CLI directly.
The npm wrapper sets this to its bundled worker.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully. Analysis warnings can still be emitted
on standard error.
.TP
.B 1
An operational error occurred, such as invalid configuration, failed analysis,
invalid artifact, or a refused file replacement.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be parsed, such as an unknown option or a missing
required argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate and validate an API document for a PHP project:
.EX
npm install --save-dev @nickwelsh/refquill
npx refquill init --language php
# Edit refquill.json to select the project's sources.
npx refquill generate
npx refquill validate docs/api.generated.json
.EE
.PP
Generate from a configuration outside the current directory:
.EX
npx refquill generate ./docs/refquill.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://docs.nickwelsh.me/refquill/docs/0.x
Refquill configuration, language support, and Fumadocs integration
.UE
